  "intro": [
    "Begin from a fresh Release 8 story with deterministic seed 1035. Enter the 69 commands in order; robot-specific commands can run while other robots continue moving. The route sets Weather Tower 2 to 100 before the third quake and finishes in 70 cycles.",
    "Verified result: 8,000 current casualties, zero projected casualties during recovery, 30,164,000 possible survivors, rank 1 (best), and the winning reset ending. There is no numeric score global; verify the ending text. This improves on Task 19.6’s no-robot-death result of 114,000 casualties and rank 3. Poet dies after sending the reset code; Waldo dies carrying the fourteen-inch cable, which Whiz retrieves and installs; Sensa dies after replacing the primary cable.",
    "Key item chain: Sensa brings the ramp and cutter; Waldo takes the grasping extension, fixes Iris, fits the red and yellow ICs, and carries the fourteen-inch cable; Iris installs that cable and the fuse; Sensa frees Fred’s twelve-inch cable and installs it in the Primary Channel; Poet carries the camera to read the sign. For seed 1035, the code is BARKLA: BAR is circle 4, KLA is circle 5. Other seeds produce a different code; use the printed halves-to-circles key.",
    "All commands are one input apiece. The deterministic route halts immediately after the second reset circle is accepted. The full local instruction trace records the exact execution count and opcode inventory."
  ],
